<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Identifying Best Fit Line for Residuals on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00741</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Identifying Best Fit Line for Residuals on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>42288089-9c84-4a5c-bae7-19daffdc409b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Each of these graphs of residuals is from the same set of data using different lines to
        fit the data. Which graph is most likely to represent the residuals from the best fit line?
        Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <table class="unnumbered" id="table-00001" summary="A 2x2 table displaying four scatter plot graphs labeled Graph A, Graph B, Graph C, and Graph D.">
  <tgroup cols="2">
    <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1"/>
    <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2"/>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <para id="para-00002"><emphasis>Graph A </emphasis>
            <media alt="A scatter plot of residuals with points at (1,1), (1,0), (1,-1), (2,0), (3,1), and (4,0) on a graph. The x-axis ranges from -1 to 4 and the y-axis from -3 to 3.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_09_01.svg"/>
            </media>
          </para>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <para id="para-00003"><emphasis>Graph B </emphasis>
            <media alt="A scatter plot of residuals on an x-y axis shows points at (1,0), (2,0), (3,0), (4,0), (2,-1), (2,-2), and (3,-1). The x-axis ranges from -1 to 4 and the y-axis from -3 to 3.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_09_02.svg"/>
            </media>
          </para>
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          <para id="para-00004"><emphasis>Graph C </emphasis>
            <media alt="A scatter plot of residuals with points at (0,0), (1,0), (2,0), (2,-1), (3,0), (3,1), and (4,2) on a coordinate plane. The x-axis ranges from -1 to 4 and the y-axis from -3 to 3.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_09_03.svg"/>
            </media>
          </para>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Graph D </emphasis>
            <media alt="A scatter plot of residuals with points at (1,1), (1,0), (2,0), (2,-1), (2.5,-2), and (3,-2). The x-axis ranges from -1 to 4 and the y-axis from -3 to 3.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_09_04.svg"/>
            </media>
          </para>
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup>
</table>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00007">Graph A is most likely to represent the residuals from the best fit line. The
            residuals seem well spaced on either side of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis without an obvious pattern,
            and all of the residuals are close to 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>